l\n96:(defn encode\n104:(defn decode\n   350\tcljs in a browser may only dial (`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/browser.cljs`).\n   351\t\n   352\t### 3.2 UDP\n   353\t\n   354\t`dao.stream.udp` is a new channel with the WebSocket deposit model: a socket\n   355\tretains nothing, so it has no reader surface, and its adapter deposits every\n   356\tdatagram as an event carrying the datagram's source address and its decoded\n   357\tvalue onto the medium the composition wired.\n   358\t\n   359\t- Descriptor: `{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/udp :dao.stream/identity\n   360\t  <channel identity> :dao.stream.udp/host h :dao.stream.udp/port p}`.\n   361\t  `attach!` binds or reuses a local socket and returns a handle whose writer\n   362\t  path is datagrams to that address.\n   363\t- One CBOR value per datagram, canonical profile. The budget covers the\n   364\t  whole encoded datagram, fragment envelope included: at most 1200 bytes,\n   365\t  the figure `dao.jing.dht.node` already uses to clear common path MTUs.\n   366\t- **Fragmentation is channel-internal.** An encoded message over budget is\n   367\t  split into `k` datagrams, each\n   368\t  `{:dao.stream.remote/id n :dao.stream.udp/part i :dao.stream.udp/parts k\n   369\t  :dao.stream.udp/bytes b}`, where `n` is the carried message's own request\n   370\t  id. The receiver reassembles by `[channel attachment identity,\n   371\t  source-address, direction, id]`, because ids are unique only per channel\n   372\t  reader and one socket may serve several attachments, and delivers only a\n   373\t  complete message. Loss of any part is loss of the whole message,\n   374\t  recovered by the link's resend rule. Reassembly is bounded by two\n   375\t  composition data, `:dao.stream.udp/max-message-bytes` (default 64 KiB)\n   376\t  and `:dao.stream.udp/max-partial-messages`, evicting the oldest partial\n   377\t  message; no clock. Neither the mirror step nor the link sees a fragment.\n   378\t- Replies go to the datagram's source address, never to an address claimed\n   379\t  in a payload.\n   380\t- A send may name an explicit destination from an already-bound socket. Hole\n   381\t  punching depends on it (section 4).\n   382\t- Unordered and best-effort. Attachment identity is the remote host and port\n   383\t  as the socket saw them; it is the reflexive address a meeting peer\n   384\t  republishes.\n   385\t\n   386\tHosts: clj (`DatagramSocket`), cljs on Node (`dgram`), cljd\n   387\t(`RawDatagramSocket`). Browsers have no UDP.\n   388\t\n   389\t### 3.3 Pair\n   260\t  \"Record `req` as outstanding under its id, with the request it was\n   261\t   sent for, its ask count, and the reflection that sent it.\"\n   262\t  [link refl req]\n   263\t  (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n   264\t    (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id]\n   265\t           {:req req :asks 0 :reflection refl})\n   266\t    (swap! refl update :ids conj id)))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn- wire-request\n   270\t  \"One request map for the channel, its id asker-minted; a next\n   271\t   request carries the link's budget when one is composed.\"\n   272\t  [link refl op args]\n   273\t  (cond-> {:dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)\n   274\t           :dao.stream.remote/op op\n   275\t           :dao.stream.remote/args args\n   276\t           :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n   277\t    (and (= :dao.stream/next op) (some? (:budget @link)))\n   278\t    (assoc :dao.stream.remote/budget (:budget @link))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn- send-request!\n   282\t  \"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\n   283\t   outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a send the\n   284\t   writer refuses with full leaves the request unsent and nothing\n   285\t   outstanding, so the operation answers as though unanswered and the\n   286\t   next ask sends again. An attach descriptor probe the writer\n   287\t   refuses with full is kept on the link instead, unsent, one retry\n   288\t   per drain until a send is accepted. Returns the writer's outcome.\"\n   289\t  [link refl req]\n   290\t  (let [r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)\n   291\t        id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n   292\t    (cond\n   293\t      (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   294\t      (do (register! link refl req)\n   295\t          (swap! link update :pending dissoc id))\n   296\t\n   297\t      (and (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   298\t           (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op req)))\n   299\t      (swap! link assoc-in [:pending id]\n   300\t             {:req req :reflection refl}))\n   301\t    r))\n   302\t\n   303\t\n   304\t(defn- count-ask!\n   305\t  \"Count one further ask of the outstanding request `id`; on reaching\n   306\t   the link's resend-after k, re-send it once -- the same id, a\n   307\t   duplicate of an idempotent operation, which recomputes the same or a\n   308\t   later, equally true answer -- and start counting afresh. append! is\n   309\t   never re-sent: it never stays outstanding beyond its send.\"\n   310\t  [link id]\n   311\t  (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   312\t    (let [k (:resend-after @link)\n   313\t          asks (inc (:asks entry))]\n   314\t      (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] asks)\n   315\t      (when (and (integer? k) (pos? k) (<= k asks))\n   316\t        (stream/append! (:writer @link) (:req entry))\n   317\t        (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] 0)))))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- outstanding-for\n   321\t  \"The id of the link's outstanding request for `op` with `arg` sent by\n   322\t   `refl`, if any; the request each outstanding id was sent for makes\n   323\t   the correlation.\"\n   324\t  [link refl op arg]\n   325\t  (when-some [[id _]\n   326\t              (first\n   327\t                (filter (fn [[_ e]]\n   328\t                          (let [r (:req e)]\n   329\t                            (and (= refl (:reflection e))\n   330\t                                 (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\n   331\t                                 (= arg (first\n   332\t                                          (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\n   333\t                        (:outstanding @link)))]\n   334\t    id))\n   335\t\n   336\t\n   337\t(defn- filed-for\n   338\t  \"The first filed answer for `op` with `arg` sent by `refl`, in id\n   339\t   order, as [id entry]. A filed answer keeps the request it was sent\n   340\t   for and the reflection that sent it -- an answer belongs to the\n   341\t   operation that caused it -- so it is found whether or not its\n   342\t   outstanding id was abandoned.\"\n   343\t  [link refl op arg]\n   344\t  (let [filed (:filed @link)]\n   345\t    (when-some [id\n   346\t                (first\n   347\t                  (filter (fn [i]\n   348\t                            (let [e (get filed i)\n   349\t                                  r (:req e)]\n   350\t                              (and (= refl (:reflection e))\n   351\t                                   (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\n   352\t                                   (= arg (first\n   353\t                                            (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\n   354\t                          (sort (keys filed))))]\n   355\t      [id (get filed id)])))\n   356\t\n   357\t\n   358\t(defn- bare-outcome\n   359\t  \"The source's own outcome map, verbatim: the correlation keys the\n   360\t   answer envelope added are removed, nothing else.\"\n   361\t  [ans]\n   362\t  (dissoc ans :dao.stream.remote/id :dao.stream/identity))\n   363\t\n   364\t\n   365\t(defn- translated\n   366\t  \"A filed protocol error at the reflection: transport-error with the\n   367\t   error's name as the reason. not-found marks the reflection gone at\n   368\t   filing; no-surface and oversize mark nothing.\"\n   369\t  [e]\n   370\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   371\t   :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t(defn- learn!\n   375\t  \"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\n   376\t   surface, plus :closable.\"\n   377\t  [refl answer]\n   378\t  (swap! refl assoc\n   379\t         :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\n   380\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n   381\t                        :closable)))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- install-more!\n   385\t  \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n   386\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n   387\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n   388\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n   389\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n   390\t   its own stream.\"\n   391\t  [link answer]\n   392\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\n   393\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n   394\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\n   395\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\n   396\t        (let [[o & further] more]\n   397\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\n   398\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- absorb!\n   402\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   403\t   id is outstanding is taken: a not-found error marks the reflection\n   404\t   gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's descriptor and\n   405\t   declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is emitted on the\n   406\t   event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is filed under its\n   407\t   id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose id is not\n   408\t   outstanding, and values that are not well-formed answers, are\n   409\t   dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   410\t  [link v]\n   411\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   412\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   413\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   414\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   415\t              req (:req entry)\n   416\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   417\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   418\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   419\t          (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   420\t          (cond\n   421\t            (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   422\t            (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   423\t                (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   424\t                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   425\t                  (emit! link v)))\n   426\t\n   427\t            (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   428\t            ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   429\t            ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   430\t            (when (nil? e)\n   431\t              (learn! refl v)\n   432\t              (emit! link v))\n   433\t\n   434\t            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   435\t            (emit! link v)\n   436\t\n   437\t            :else\n   438\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   439\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   440\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\n   441\t\n   442\t\n   443\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   444\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   445\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   446\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   447\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   448\t  [link]\n   449\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   450\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   451\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   452\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   453\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   454\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   455\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn- retry-pending!\n   459\t  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n   460\t   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n   461\t   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n   462\t  [link]\n   463\t  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n   464\t    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n   465\t\n   466\t\n   467\t(defn- drain!\n   468\t  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n   469\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n   470\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n   471\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n   472\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n   473\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n   474\t   one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n   475\t   is accepted.\"\n   476\t  [link]\n   477\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   478\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n   479\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n   480\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 10:32:54 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 17:32:54 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nP1 | [udp.cljc:295](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:295) | Reassembly rejects a message when `parts × 1200` exceeds 64 KiB, even if its actual encoded payload is within the 64 KiB limit. The 48 KiB test passes, but valid messages nearer the limit can be sent and then dropped. | Bound accumulated chunk bytes and check the completed payload’s actual length.\n\nP1 | [jvm.clj:24](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/clj/dao/stream/udp/jvm.clj:24) | The receiver reuses one `DatagramPacket` without resetting its length. After a short datagram, a later longer datagram can be truncated, losing a message or fragment. | Reset the packet length to the buffer length before each receive.\n\nP2 | [udp.cljc:292](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc:292) | Fragment fields are used without validation. A malformed `parts`, `part`, or `bytes` value can throw during reassembly; on Node and Dart, the adapter callback does not catch that error. | Validate fragment types, ranges, and byte payloads before changing partial state; drop malformed datagrams.\n\nThe added direction field resolves the request/answer collision described by the implementer. Choosing 64 for the unspecified partial-message default and using a shared deposit medium with per-attachment forwarding are reasonable readings of §3.2. The two receive defects prevent sign-off despite the supplied passing suites.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
